@.str.169 = private unnamed_addr constant [833 x i8] c"Computes the mesh that encompasses the union of the volumes of two meshes.\0ABoth meshes should be manifold.\0A\0AThis function always uses the CPU device.\0A\0AArgs:\0A    mesh (open3d.t.geometry.TriangleMesh): This is the second operand for the\0A        boolean operation.\0A\0A    tolerance (float): Threshold which determines when point distances are\0A        considered to be 0.\0A\0AReturns:\0A    The mesh describing the union volume.\0A\0AExample:\0A    This computes the union of a sphere and a cube::\0A\0A        box = o3d.geometry.TriangleMesh.create_box()\0A        box = o3d.t.geometry.TriangleMesh.from_legacy(box)\0A        sphere = o3d.geometry.TriangleMesh.create_sphere(0.8)\0A        sphere = o3d.t.geometry.TriangleMesh.from_legacy(sphere)\0A\0A        ans = box.boolean_union(sphere)\0A\0A        o3d.visualization.draw([{'name': 'union', 'geometry': ans}])\0A\00", align 1
