@.str.213 = private unnamed_addr constant [926 x i8] c"Returns a new mesh with the vertices selected according to the indices list.\0AIf an item from the indices list exceeds the max vertex number of the mesh\0Aor has a negative value, it is ignored.\0A\0AArgs:\0A    indices (open3d.core.Tensor): An integer list of indices. Duplicates are\0A    allowed, but ignored. Signed and unsigned integral types are accepted.\0A    copy_attributes (bool): Indicates if vertex attributes (other than\0A    positions) and triangle attributes (other than indices) should be copied to\0A    the returned mesh.\0A\0AReturns:\0A    A new mesh with the selected vertices and faces built from these vertices.\0A    If the original mesh is empty, return an empty mesh.\0A\0AExample:\0A\0A    This code selects the top face of a box, which has indices [2, 3, 6, 7]::\0A\0A        import open3d as o3d\0A        import numpy as np\0A        box = o3d.t.geometry.TriangleMesh.create_box()\0A        top_face = box.select_by_index([2, 3, 6, 7])\0A\00", align 1
