@.str.219 = private unnamed_addr constant [1078 x i8] c"\0ACreate an albedo for the triangle mesh using calibrated images. The triangle\0Amesh must have texture coordinates (\22texture_uvs\22 triangle attribute). This works\0Aby back projecting the images onto the texture surface. Overlapping images are\0Ablended together in the resulting albedo. For best results, use images captured\0Awith exposure and white balance lock to reduce the chance of seams in the output\0Atexture.\0A\0AThis function is only supported on the CPU.\0A\0AArgs:\0A    images (List[open3d.t.geometry.Image]): List of images.\0A    intrinsic_matrices (List[open3d.core.Tensor]): List of (3,3) intrinsic matrices describing\0A        the pinhole camera.\0A    extrinsic_matrices (List[open3d.core.Tensor]): List of (4,4) extrinsic matrices describing\0A        the position and orientation of the camera.\0A    tex_size (int): Output albedo texture size. This is a square image, so\0A        only one side is needed.\0A    update_material (bool): Whether to update the material of the triangle\0A        mesh, possibly overwriting an existing albedo texture.\0A\0AReturns:\0A    Image with albedo texture.\00", align 1
