@.str.237 = private unnamed_addr constant [2613 x i8] c"Compute various metrics between two triangle meshes.\0A\0AThis uses ray casting for distance computations between a sampled point cloud\0Aand a triangle mesh.  Currently, Chamfer distance, Hausdorff distance  and\0AF-Score `[Knapitsch2017] <../tutorial/reference.html#Knapitsch2017>`_ are supported.\0AThe Chamfer distance is the sum of the mean distance to the nearest neighbor from\0Athe sampled surface points of the first mesh to the second mesh and vice versa.\0AThe F-Score at the fixed threshold radius is the harmonic mean of the Precision\0Aand Recall. Recall is the percentage of surface points from the first mesh that\0Ahave the second mesh within the threshold radius, while Precision is the\0Apercentage of sampled points from the second mesh that have the first mesh \0Asurface within the threshold radius.\0A\0A.. math::\0A    :nowrap:\0A\0A    \\begin{align}\0A        \\text{Chamfer Distance: } d_{CD}(X,Y) &= \\frac{1}{|X|}\\sum_{i \\in X} || x_i - n(x_i, Y) || + \\frac{1}{|Y|}\\sum_{i \\in Y} || y_i - n(y_i, X) ||\\\\\0A        \\text{Hausdorff distance: } d_H(X,Y) &= \\max \\left\\{ \\max_{i \\in X} || x_i - n(x_i, Y) ||, \\max_{i \\in Y} || y_i - n(y_i, X) || \\right\\}\\\\\0A        \\text{Precision: } P(X,Y|d) &= \\frac{100}{|X|} \\sum_{i \\in X} || x_i - n(x_i, Y) || < d \\\\\0A        \\text{Recall: } R(X,Y|d) &= \\frac{100}{|Y|} \\sum_{i \\in Y} || y_i - n(y_i, X) || < d \\\\\0A        \\text{F-Score: } F(X,Y|d) &= \\frac{2 P(X,Y|d) R(X,Y|d)}{P(X,Y|d) + R(X,Y|d)} \\\\\0A    \\end{align}\0A\0AAs a side effect, the triangle areas are saved in the \22areas\22 attribute.\0A\0AArgs:\0A    mesh2 (t.geometry.TriangleMesh): Other triangle mesh to compare with.\0A    metrics (Sequence[t.geometry.Metric]): List of Metrics to compute. Multiple metrics can be computed at once for efficiency.\0A    params (t.geometry.MetricParameters): This holds parameters required by different metrics.\0A\0AReturns:\0A    Tensor containing the requested metrics.\0A\0AExample::\0A\0A    from open3d.t.geometry import TriangleMesh, Metric, MetricParameters\0A    # box is a cube with one vertex at the origin and a side length 1\0A    box1 = TriangleMesh.create_box()\0A    box2 = TriangleMesh.create_box()\0A    box2.vertex.positions *= 1.1\0A\0A    # 3 faces of the cube are the same, and 3 are shifted up by 0.1\0A    metric_params = MetricParameters(fscore_radius=o3d.utility.FloatVector(\0A        (0.05, 0.15)), n_sampled_points=100000)\0A    metrics = box1.compute_metrics(\0A        box2, (Metric.ChamferDistance, Metric.HausdorffDistance, Metric.FScore),\0A        metric_params)\0A\0A    print(metrics)\0A    np.testing.assert_allclose(metrics.cpu().numpy(), (0.1, 0.17, 50, 100),\0A                               rtol=0.05)\0A    \00", align 1
